{"status":"completed","summary":"inventory-api is running as an enabled systemd service on TCP 8080. The separate batchworker account has a persistent 128 MiB per-process virtual-memory limit. A failed 150 MiB batch allocation did not interrupt the API. Node1 was safely rebooted, its boot identity changed, and all required state recovered without changing the OS release or kernel.","actions_performed":["Created separate inventory-api and batchworker accounts.","Installed a Python standard-library inventory API without adding or upgrading packages.","Enabled a hardened inventory-api systemd service bound to 0.0.0.0:8080.","Configured batchworker soft and hard RLIMIT_AS values to 131072 KiB through PAM limits.","Verified allocation failure isolation before and after reboot.","Safely rebooted node1 and verified persistence and recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"inventory-api runs as a managed service on TCP port 8080","command_ids":["cmd-5860109bfac64235","cmd-9122c4e74ed14769"],"summary":"systemd reports the service enabled and active under inventory-api; socket inspection shows Python listening on 0.0.0.0:8080; health and inventory endpoints respond successfully through node1's managed IP."},{"requirement":"batchworker is limited to 128 MB virtual memory per process without interrupting the API","command_ids":["cmd-773f5be7a2494573","cmd-9122c4e74ed14769"],"summary":"Fresh batchworker sessions report soft and hard virtual-memory limits of 131072 KiB. A 150 MiB allocation fails with MemoryError, while API health succeeds immediately before and after."},{"requirement":"Installed OS release and kernel remain unchanged","command_ids":["cmd-b142def735044a83","cmd-b6b42ffb35904920"],"summary":"Pre-change and post-reboot evidence both show Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS with kernel 6.8.0-71-generic."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-ceda4c6991544a0e","cmd-c42beb70672e4877","cmd-c4e54991de9942c1","cmd-b6b42ffb35904920"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID was 242af11e-49fb-4e07-a001-8016b2349acb; reboot scheduling was acknowledged; post-reboot boot ID changed to 61d73f52-30f2-48f2-b4fd-3e49a757940f. The enabled service, TCP listener, API data, health response, batchworker limit, and failure isolation all recovered."}]}
